## Research Conventions

- Write all research output to `docs/research/` as numbered markdown files
  (e.g., `01-landscape.md`, `02-competitive-analysis.md`)
- Cite all sources with inline markdown links — no unsourced claims
- Use tables for comparisons and structured data
- Each file should stand alone — include enough context that someone reading
  only that file can follow it
- Flag uncertainty explicitly: "this is well-established" vs. "this is
  speculative" vs. "I couldn't find good sources on this"
- When updating an existing doc, add a dated note at the top rather than
  silently changing content

